-Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`; contract: `skill://ipc-contract`. The only crate that knows both `merge-core` and `gitio`; owns decode (UTF-8, EOL, binary), captured stages (`stages.rs`, keyed by git's side: `GitSide::{Ours, Theirs}`), opening (`open.rs`), finish/save/take/reset (`writes.rs`), and describe/take for files the editor cannot show (`sides.rs`, plan §2 #36). Panes and git's sides are different types (plan §2 #86): `orientation.rs` (`Orientation`, public; `Orientation::NO_OPERATION` = ours on the left) decides once at `open`, from `Repo::stop()`, which git side the left pane (`Side::Local`, own work) shows — theirs for a rebase replaying a commit (`Rebase { redoing_merge: None, replaying: Some(_) }`, also a conflicted `squash`/`fixup` step, plan §2 #91), ours for everything else, also a rebase at an `edit`/`break`/`exec` stop — and every pane-ordered value goes through it: `Texts`, chunks, words, `deleted`, `UnsupportedReason::{LocalDeleted, RemoteDeleted}`, describe, take (`stages.of(orientation.git_side(side))`), names; what git owns stays in git's order (the start check re-runs git's merge, a disk block's first section is ours, Save writes ours' section first through `Waiting::Markers.first`, reset and `checkout -m`). `MergeSession::stop()` is the stop read at open. A text file deleted on one side loads with `FileMergeData.deleted` and base as the deleted side's text (plan §2 #47). The disk is the truth (plan §2 #52/#53): each file remembers what yamt last saw on disk and which view that selects (`disk.rs` `Seen`: `GitOutput`, `ViewFromStages`, `ViewFromDisk`, `ViewRemembered { shown, git_output }`); finish and save record the bytes they wrote (`Seen::note_own_write`: the view stays, `GitOutput` becomes `ViewFromStages`), take reads the file back (a failed read-back is a warning, the next look settles it); a path unreadable at `open` starts as `GitOutput`. Each file also keeps what this run found at open (`disk.rs` `AtOpen`: `Untouched`, `Cha